  "fairness": {
    "conventionalAdvantage": "The page path returns a payload carrying a hash, a declared height range and an error figure; the network returns point values and nothing else, so equal latency is not equal product.",
    "neuralAdvantage": "The page path reads and decompresses whole pages for any query, so a one-sample request costs a 65x65 page. The network evaluates exactly the points asked for, which is the whole structural case for a coordinate representation and is what readAmplification quantifies."
  },
  "guard": null,
  "qualification": "Decode cost for point queries. Not mesh construction, not upload, not whole-frame behaviour, and not the cold-start cost of loading weights unless cacheState says so.",
